.TH KINGCOBRA 1 "November 2026" "KingCobra 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kingcobra, kc \- the KingCobra programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kingcobra
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B kingcobra
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile.kc\fR [\fIscript args\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs, checks, tests and debugs KingCobra programs. With no arguments on a terminal it starts the REPL.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fIfile.kc\fR
Run a program (a bare file.kc means the same).
.TP
.B repl [\fIfile.kc\fR]
Interactive session.
.TP
.B eval \fIcode\fR
Run a snippet given on the command line.
.TP
.B check \fIpath\fR...
Parse and type-check without running.
.TP
.B test [\fIpath\fR...]
Run every test_* function.
.TP
.B new \fIname\fR, init
Create a project.
.TP
.B info
Version, platform, features and search paths.
.TP
.B modules
List the standard-library modules.
.TP
.B help [\fItopic\fR]
Show help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-jit
Never compile hot functions to machine code; use the interpreter only.
.TP
.BI \-I " DIR"
Add DIR to the #include search path.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-typecheck
Skip the static type checker.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KC_JIT=0
Same as \-\-no\-jit.
.TP
.B KC_INCLUDE
Colon-separated #include search path.
.SH NOTES
The closure JIT exists on x86-64 only; on ARM64, ARMhf, RISC-V and other CPUs programs run in the interpreter with identical results.
Run \fBkingcobra help\fR for the complete, current option list.
